# Simulator build/run artifacts (VCS/Questa via cocotb Makefile.sim), for
# EVERY per-block bench dir (b3e8e99 accidentally committed one block's
# sim_build tree via `git add -A`; bd7e912 untracked it and added a local
# tests/mdio_phy_model/.gitignore — this file generalizes that to all
# benches, incl. the new sim_smoke).
sim_build/
sim_build_fake/
# Bench variants that build a second simv with different params (clcd's
# READP=1 read-path pass -> sim_build_readpath/results_readpath.xml; the
# csr_decode_width per-block/mutant dirs -> sim_build_<block>...). No
# sim_build_* variant is ever a source file.
sim_build_*/
# Mutated RTL written by a "must fail" control target (tests/dfx_ctl's
# control-wdt-unclamp, tests/usr_access_rd's control-decode). A control has to
# build the BROKEN RTL to be worth anything, and that RTL must never be mistaken
# for a source file -- which is exactly how a mutant gets committed and then
# read as the design.
mutant/
results.xml
results_fake.xml
results_readpath.xml
ucli.key
*.vcd
*.fsdb
*.daidir/
csrc/
vc_hdrs.h
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
# VCS code-coverage artifacts (make COVERAGE=1 / make coverage — A5)
cov_*.vdb/
cov_report/
cov_report_urg.log
urgReport/
cov_build.log
cov_urg.log
*.cm.log
*.vdb.uf

# transient sim artifacts
nanosoc.f
*.out
